1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,400
You looked at shoes. Once.

2
00:00:01,400 --> 00:00:02,600
Now they are everywhere.

3
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:04,200
That is NOT the app reading your mind.

4
00:00:04,200 --> 00:00:06,000
It is ONE small file. A COOKIE.

5
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:08,200
A COOKIE is a NOTE a site leaves in your browser.

6
00:00:08,200 --> 00:00:10,400
It says: this is the SAME person as before.

7
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:12,000
That is useful. It is how a login stays logged in.

8
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:14,200
Now imagine the SAME NOTE on a second site.

9
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:16,200
SAME company on both sites.

10
00:00:16,200 --> 00:00:18,400
TWO visits. ONE identity. That is the trick.

11
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:20,000
That is what a THIRD-PARTY COOKIE is.

12
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:22,400
The NOTE carries a NUMBER. Not your name.

13
00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:24,600
INCOGNITO does NOT stop this. It forgets on your device, NOT theirs.

14
00:00:24,600 --> 00:00:26,600
Which is why you see the shoes, NOT the exact pair you picked.

15
00:00:26,600 --> 00:00:29,000
The standard says it plainly, and calls it worrisome.

16
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:31,000
Safari, Firefox and Brave block these by default.

17
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:33,000
Apps run their own version. The SWITCH is in your phone settings.

18
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:35,000
If you are NOT on ONE of those, this is the switch.

19
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:36,800
Blocking them rarely breaks anything. A few logins get grumpier.

20
00:00:36,800 --> 00:00:38,800
You do NOT need to understand all of it to turn it off.

21
00:00:38,800 --> 00:00:41,200
ONE NOTE. Every site. ONE switch.

22
00:00:41,200 --> 00:00:43,000
NOTE. Shared. Blocked.

23
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:45,000
The shoes cannot follow you if the NOTE cannot travel.
